<LessonPage page={page}>
<main class="wrap" data-core-duration="70–80 minutes" data-extension-duration="15–20 minutes">
  <p class="kicker"><span class="dot"></span> Grammar and discourse · Lesson 11</p>
  <h1>Advanced discourse markers: <em>make the logic visible, not heavier</em></h1>
  <p class="standfirst">A discourse marker is a promise about the relationship between ideas. <span class="ex">Nevertheless</span> promises a counterexpectation, <span class="ex">therefore</span> presents an inference, and <span class="ex">in other words</span> promises a reformulation. The marker does not create the relationship or prove the claim. First map the move; then choose the form, position, punctuation, register, and spoken prominence that help the listener follow it.</p>
  <div class="meta-row"><span class="tag">70–80 min core</span><span class="tag">relation → evidence → marker</span><span class="tag">position, punctuation, and register</span><span class="tag">15–20 min listening and retrieval</span></div>
  <div class="lesson-flow" aria-label="Lesson flow"><div class="flow-step"><b>Map</b><span>Name the exact relation.</span></div><div class="flow-step"><b>Test</b><span>Check whether the evidence licenses it.</span></div><div class="flow-step"><b>Signal</b><span>Choose form, position, and register.</span></div><div class="flow-step"><b>Sustain</b><span>Guide a listener without overmarking.</span></div></div>
  <p class="note-line"><b>Can-do:</b> By the end, you can distinguish addition, comparison, concession, counterexpectation, direct correction, consequence, inference, exemplification, specification, reformulation, scope, and conclusion; build sentence connectors, subordinators, prepositional patterns, and parallel pairs; punctuate initial, medial, and semicolon-linked connectors; distinguish contrastive <span class="ex">however</span> from <span class="ex">however + adjective/adverb</span>; use <span class="ex">thereby + -ing</span> accurately; choose formal, neutral, and conversational signposts; hear a marker as a separate thought group or an integrated light parenthetical; avoid connector density; and organize a source-based argument whose relations remain no stronger than the evidence.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You recovered B1 cause, result, concession, phrase structure, and dependable however punctuation before making finer B2 choices.">
    <h3>Reactivate five dependable linker patterns</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Discourse foundation choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="because">because</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="so">so</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Although">Although</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Despite">Despite</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="However,">However,</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="because of">because of</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The room closed early <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="because" data-hint="A finite clause with subject and verb follows the gap." data-fix="The room closed early because the alarm failed.">choose</button> the alarm failed.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The alarm failed, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="so" data-hint="Join the cause to its stated result inside one sentence." data-fix="The alarm failed, so the room closed early.">choose</button> the room closed early.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Although" data-hint="A full finite clause follows this concessive subordinator." data-fix="Although the trial was short, it revealed a useful pattern.">choose</button> the trial was short, it revealed a useful pattern.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Despite" data-hint="A noun phrase, the short trial, follows the gap." data-fix="Despite the short trial, the team found a useful pattern.">choose</button> the short trial, the team found a useful pattern.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The trial was short. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="However," data-hint="Use a sentence connector with a comma after the opening chunk." data-fix="The trial was short. However, it revealed a useful pattern.">choose</button> it revealed a useful pattern.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Notice: one record, six logical moves</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Fictional Westbridge evening hub proposal</h3>
    <p><span class="ex">Admittedly, the eight-week trial was short. Nevertheless, the attendance record supports a longer test.</span> The first marker accepts a real limitation; the second presents a result that remains worth considering despite it.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">The hub averaged 46 visits per evening. Furthermore, 51 of 68 survey respondents reported having a quieter place to work.</span> The survey adds support, but it does not repair the limits of a self-selected sample.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">The trial had no comparison site; therefore, it cannot establish that the hub caused changes in employment or exam results.</span> The second proposition is an inference licensed by the missing comparison.</p>
    <p><span class="ex">In other words, the record supports a longer measured trial, not a permanent citywide program. On balance, a twelve-month extension at the same annex is defensible.</span> One marker reformulates the scope; the other signals a conclusion after weighing support and limits.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You identified concession, counterexpectation, addition, evidence-limited inference, reformulation, and balanced conclusion without letting a marker manufacture proof.">
    <h3>Discovery check: relation, evidence, and strength</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Discourse discovery choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="accepts the short duration as a real limitation">accepts the short duration as a real limitation</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="keeps the longer test worth considering despite that limitation">keeps the longer test worth considering despite that limitation</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="adds an independent survey result">adds an independent survey result</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="infers a limit on causal claims">infers a limit on causal claims</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="restates the supported scope more clearly">restates the supported scope more clearly</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="signals a weighed conclusion">signals a weighed conclusion</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="proves every claim placed after it">proves every claim placed after it</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><span class="ex">Admittedly</span> <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="accepts the short duration as a real limitation" data-hint="The writer grants rather than denies the weakness." data-fix="Admittedly accepts the short duration as a real limitation.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><span class="ex">Nevertheless</span> <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="keeps the longer test worth considering despite that limitation" data-hint="The conclusion survives a previously accepted obstacle." data-fix="Nevertheless introduces the counterexpectation that a longer test remains worth considering.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><span class="ex">Furthermore</span> <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="adds an independent survey result" data-hint="The next fact supports the same direction rather than opposing it." data-fix="Furthermore adds the separate survey result.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span><span class="ex">Therefore</span> <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="infers a limit on causal claims" data-hint="No comparison site supports a conclusion about what cannot yet be established." data-fix="Therefore presents the evidence-based inference that causal claims are limited.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><span class="ex">In other words</span> <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="restates the supported scope more clearly" data-hint="The writer translates the evidence boundary into a practical distinction." data-fix="In other words reformulates the supported scope.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span><span class="ex">On balance</span> <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="signals a weighed conclusion" data-hint="The writer has considered both support and limitations." data-fix="On balance signals a conclusion reached after weighing competing considerations.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Get to the root: name the move before the marker</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Move</th><th>What the next idea does</th><th>Useful signals</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>addition or reinforcement</td><td>adds support in the same direction</td><td>furthermore, moreover, in addition, also</td></tr>
    <tr><td>comparison or contrast</td><td>compares two distinct cases or qualities</td><td>whereas, by contrast, on the other hand</td></tr>
    <tr><td>concession</td><td>accepts a point that could weaken the position</td><td>admittedly, granted, although, despite</td></tr>
    <tr><td>counterexpectation</td><td>shows that a conclusion survives the conceded obstacle</td><td>nevertheless, nonetheless, even so, still</td></tr>
    <tr><td>direct correction</td><td>rejects a proposition and states its opposite</td><td>on the contrary, rather</td></tr>
    <tr><td>consequence or inference</td><td>presents what follows from the previous basis</td><td>therefore, consequently, thus, as a result</td></tr>
    <tr><td>example or specification</td><td>illustrates a class or names the exact member</td><td>for example, in particular, namely</td></tr>
    <tr><td>reformulation</td><td>restates or sharpens substantially the same message</td><td>in other words, more precisely, that is</td></tr>
    <tr><td>stance or scope</td><td>limits the angle, strength, or domain of a claim</td><td>to some extent, in principle, in practice, from this perspective</td></tr>
    <tr><td>weighed conclusion</td><td>closes after considering more than one factor</td><td>on balance, overall, all things considered</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <div class="note"><h3>Concession is a two-move relationship</h3><p><span class="ex">Admittedly, the trial was short. Nevertheless, it was useful.</span> First accept a relevant obstacle; then state the counterexpectation. <span class="ex">However</span> can signal the turn too, but a marker does not make a weak counterclaim convincing. The second claim still needs support.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3><span class="ex">On the contrary</span> is not a formal version of <span class="ex">however</span></h3><p>Use it to reject a proposition directly: <span class="ex">The hub was not empty. On the contrary, it averaged 46 visits per evening.</span> For two different features, use contrast: <span class="ex">The annex is centrally located, whereas the north site has more parking.</span></p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You mapped addition, contrast, concession, counterexpectation, correction, inference, example, specification, reformulation, and conclusion from complete contexts.">
    <h3>Choose ten exact logical moves</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Discourse relation choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Furthermore">Furthermore</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="whereas">whereas</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Admittedly">Admittedly</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Even so">Even so</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="On the contrary">On the contrary</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Therefore">Therefore</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="For example">For example</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="namely">namely</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="In other words">In other words</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="On balance">On balance</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Meanwhile">Meanwhile</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The logs show regular attendance. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Furthermore" data-hint="Add a second supporting fact in the same direction." data-fix="Furthermore, the accessibility audit found no entrance barrier.">choose</button>, the accessibility audit found no entrance barrier.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The annex is near three bus routes, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="whereas" data-hint="Compare one complete clause with a different feature of another site." data-fix="The annex is near three bus routes, whereas the north site has more parking.">choose</button> the north site has more parking.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Admittedly" data-hint="Open by granting a relevant limitation." data-fix="Admittedly, the survey was self-selected.">choose</button>, the survey was self-selected.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>Only 68 users answered the survey. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Even so" data-hint="The next claim remains valid despite that obstacle." data-fix="Even so, the responses identify questions worth testing in a longer trial.">choose</button>, the responses identify questions worth testing in a longer trial.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The hub was not empty. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="On the contrary" data-hint="Reject the preceding negative proposition with directly opposing evidence." data-fix="On the contrary, it averaged 46 visits per evening.">choose</button>, it averaged 46 visits per evening.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The trial had no comparison site. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Therefore" data-hint="Infer a defensible limit from the missing comparison." data-fix="Therefore, the record cannot establish that the hub caused later outcomes.">choose</button>, the record cannot establish that the hub caused later outcomes.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>The next trial should measure access barriers. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="For example" data-hint="Introduce one illustration of the broader class." data-fix="For example, the city could record elevator outages.">choose</button>, the city could record elevator outages.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>The committee approved one location, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="namely" data-hint="Identify the exact member rather than merely illustrating a possible one." data-fix="The committee approved one location, namely the old library annex.">choose</button> the old library annex.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>The evidence supports extending the test but not generalizing beyond the site. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="In other words" data-hint="Restate the same boundary as a practical recommendation." data-fix="In other words, continue at the annex without claiming a citywide result.">choose</button>, continue at the annex without claiming a citywide result.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>The record shows useful demand but important limits. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="On balance" data-hint="Signal a conclusion reached after weighing both sides." data-fix="On balance, a measured twelve-month extension is defensible.">choose</button>, a measured twelve-month extension is defensible.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Build the clause, position, and punctuation accurately</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <table><thead><tr><th>Grammar</th><th>Dependable pattern</th><th>Example</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td>sentence connector</td><td>sentence. Connector, sentence.</td><td>The trial was short. Nevertheless, it was useful.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>semicolon-linked connector</td><td>sentence; connector, sentence.</td><td>The trial was short; nevertheless, it was useful.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>integrated parenthetical</td><td>subject, connector, predicate.</td><td>The trial, however, revealed a useful pattern.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>subordinator</td><td>although/even though + finite clause</td><td>Although the trial was short, it was useful.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>preposition</td><td>despite/in spite of + noun or -ing</td><td>Despite its short duration, it was useful.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>concessive degree</td><td>however + adjective/adverb + clause</td><td>However short the trial was, it revealed a pattern.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>resulting means</td><td>clause, thereby + -ing</td><td>The city added evening hours, thereby improving access.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>paired reinforcement</td><td>not only + parallel A, but also + parallel B</td><td>The hub not only extended hours but also added workstations.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <div class="note"><h3>Contrastive <span class="ex">however</span> and concessive <span class="ex">however</span> have different syntax</h3><p><span class="ex">However, the trial was useful</span> uses a connector followed by a comma. <span class="ex">However short the trial was, it was useful</span> means “no matter how short”; do not insert a comma immediately after <span class="ex">however</span>. <span class="ex">The trial, however, was useful</span> integrates a parenthetical turn inside the clause.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Position changes scope and rhythm</h3><p>Initial <span class="ex">therefore</span> frames the whole next sentence. Medial <span class="ex">therefore</span> can stay close to the inference: <span class="ex">The sample is narrow and therefore cannot support a citywide claim.</span> Do not move a marker mechanically if the new position makes its scope unclear.</p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You controlled finite clauses, noun phrases, sentence boundaries, medial punctuation, concessive however, thereby plus -ing, and parallel reinforcement.">
    <h3>Complete eleven form, position, and punctuation decisions</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Discourse form choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Although the trial was short">Although the trial was short</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Despite its short duration">Despite its short duration</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="However, it revealed a useful pattern">However, it revealed a useful pattern</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="however,">however,</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="however short the trial was">however short the trial was</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="therefore cannot support">therefore cannot support</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="thereby improving">thereby improving</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="not only extended the hours but also added workstations">not only extended the hours but also added workstations</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Although the trial was short, it was useful">Although the trial was short, it was useful</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="The trial was short; nevertheless, it was useful">The trial was short; nevertheless, it was useful</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Despite the fact that the trial was short">Despite the fact that the trial was short</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Despite the trial was short">Despite the trial was short</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Although the trial was short" data-hint="Use a subordinator before the finite clause the trial was short." data-fix="Although the trial was short, it produced a useful attendance record.">choose</button>, it produced a useful attendance record.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Despite its short duration" data-hint="Use a preposition before the noun phrase its short duration." data-fix="Despite its short duration, the trial produced a useful attendance record.">choose</button>, the trial produced a useful attendance record.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The trial was short. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="However, it revealed a useful pattern" data-hint="Begin a new sentence with a connector, comma, subject, and predicate." data-fix="The trial was short. However, it revealed a useful pattern.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The trial, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="however," data-hint="Close the medial parenthetical with its second comma." data-fix="The trial, however, revealed a useful pattern.">choose</button> revealed a useful pattern.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span><button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="however short the trial was" data-hint="Build the no-matter-how pattern without a comma after however." data-fix="However short the trial was, it revealed a useful pattern.">choose</button>, it revealed a useful pattern.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The sample is self-selected and <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="therefore cannot support" data-hint="Place the inference marker before the coordinated verb phrase it scopes over." data-fix="The sample is self-selected and therefore cannot support a population estimate.">choose</button> a population estimate.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>The city added evening hours, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="thereby improving" data-hint="Thereby is followed by an -ing form that names the result produced by the action." data-fix="The city added evening hours, thereby improving access for daytime workers.">choose</button> access for daytime workers.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>The hub <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="not only extended the hours but also added workstations" data-hint="Keep both coordinated verb phrases parallel after the paired marker." data-fix="The hub not only extended the hours but also added workstations.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>Choose the complete sentence with one concessive subordinator and no double conjunction: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Although the trial was short, it was useful" data-hint="Although already marks the relationship, so do not add but." data-fix="Although the trial was short, it was useful.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>Choose the complete semicolon pattern: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="The trial was short; nevertheless, it was useful" data-hint="Use a semicolon between independent clauses and a comma after the connector." data-fix="The trial was short; nevertheless, it was useful.">choose</button>.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">11</span><span>Keep <span class="ex">despite</span> before a finite clause by adding a noun frame: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Despite the fact that the trial was short" data-hint="The fact is the noun complement of despite; that introduces the finite clause." data-fix="Despite the fact that the trial was short, it was useful.">choose</button>, it was useful.</span></div>
    <div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-choices>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-choices>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <h2>Keep neighboring functions and registers separate</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>A result marker presents reasoning; it does not certify causation</h3><p><span class="ex">The trial lacked a comparison site. Therefore, it cannot establish causation</span> is defensible. <span class="ex">Attendance rose. Therefore, the hub caused employment growth</span> is not supported by the record. If the logical bridge is uncertain, qualify it: <span class="ex">This may have contributed to...</span> or state the two facts without a causal marker.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Reformulation, specification, and example promise different things</h3><p><span class="ex">In other words</span> restates substantially the same message. <span class="ex">More precisely</span> narrows or corrects the wording. <span class="ex">Namely</span> identifies an exact member or list. <span class="ex">For example</span> gives one illustration and does not claim it is the only one.</p></div>
  <div class="note"><h3>Longer and more formal does not mean more advanced</h3><p><span class="ex">Moreover</span> and <span class="ex">furthermore</span> fit formal reinforcement; <span class="ex">also</span> is widely neutral. In conversation, <span class="ex">but, still, so, actually, I mean</span>, and <span class="ex">at the same time</span> often guide a listener more naturally. Selective signposting is advanced. A marker in every sentence can obscure hierarchy and sound rehearsed.</p></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You separated inference, mechanism, example, exact specification, reformulation, precision, formal reinforcement, spoken counterpoint, principle-practice contrast, and optional zero marking.">
    <h3>Choose ten meaning and register boundaries</h3>
    <div class="choice-bank" aria-label="Discourse boundary choices"><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Therefore">Therefore</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="thereby">thereby</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="For example">For example</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="namely">namely</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="In other words">In other words</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="More precisely">More precisely</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Furthermore">Furthermore</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="Still">Still</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="In practice">In practice</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="no additional marker">no additional marker</button><button class="choice-option" data-choice-option="On the contrary">On the contrary</button></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">1</span><span>The sample is self-selected. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Therefore" data-hint="Present the next sentence as a warranted inference from that sampling limit." data-fix="Therefore, the percentage cannot represent every hub user.">choose</button>, the percentage cannot represent every hub user.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">2</span><span>The city extended the hours, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="thereby" data-hint="Name a result produced through the preceding action before an -ing form." data-fix="The city extended the hours, thereby allowing daytime workers to attend.">choose</button> allowing daytime workers to attend.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">3</span><span>The next trial should record access barriers. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="For example" data-hint="Give one nonexhaustive illustration." data-fix="For example, it could record elevator outages.">choose</button>, it could record elevator outages.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">4</span><span>The committee approved one site, <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="namely" data-hint="Identify the exact site included in the decision." data-fix="The committee approved one site, namely the old library annex.">choose</button> the old library annex.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">5</span><span>The evidence supports continuation but not expansion. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="In other words" data-hint="Restate the same scope in clearer practical terms." data-fix="In other words, keep testing at the annex before making a citywide claim.">choose</button>, keep testing at the annex before making a citywide claim.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">6</span><span>The program was popular. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="More precisely" data-hint="Narrow the broad adjective popular to the exact attendance fact." data-fix="More precisely, it averaged 46 visits per evening.">choose</button>, it averaged 46 visits per evening.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">7</span><span>In a formal report, add a second independent benefit: <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Furthermore" data-hint="Choose the formal reinforcement marker rather than a contradiction marker." data-fix="Furthermore, the evening schedule improved access for daytime workers.">choose</button>, the evening schedule improved access for daytime workers.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">8</span><span>In a conversation, accept the short trial but keep the result useful: “It was only eight weeks. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="Still" data-hint="Use the compact conversational counterexpectation marker." data-fix="Still, it gives us a reason to test the idea longer.">choose</button>, it gives us a reason to test the idea longer.”</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">9</span><span>The policy promises equal access on paper. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="In practice" data-hint="Contrast an abstract design with what actually happens." data-fix="In practice, elevator outages sometimes block the second floor.">choose</button>, elevator outages sometimes block the second floor.</span></div>
    <div class="q"><span class="n">10</span><span>The second sentence simply continues the same clearly ordered description: “The doors opened at six. <button class="choice-gap" data-choice-gap data-answer="no additional marker" data-hint="Do not add a signpost when chronology and sentence order already make the link clear." data-fix="The doors opened at six. Forty-six people arrived during the evening. No additional marker is necessary.">choose</button> Forty-six people arrived during the evening.”</span></div>
