    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="It operated Monday through Thursday from 6:00 to 10:00 p.m." data-hint="Recover the four named weekdays and evening hours." data-fix="It operated Monday through Thursday from 6:00 to 10:00 p.m."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which schedule can a report specify exactly?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It operated Monday through Thursday from 6:00 to 10:00 p.m.">It operated Monday through Thursday from 6:00 to 10:00 p.m.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It remained open twenty-four hours every day.">It remained open twenty-four hours every day.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="It opened only on weekend mornings.">It opened only on weekend mornings.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Entry logs recorded an average of 46 visits per evening, but they did not identify unique repeat visitors." data-hint="Keep the observed average and the tracking limitation together." data-fix="The logs recorded 46 visits per evening on average but did not identify unique repeat visitors."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which attendance claim preserves the log's limit?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Entry logs recorded an average of 46 visits per evening, but they did not identify unique repeat visitors.">Entry logs recorded an average of 46 visits per evening, but they did not identify unique repeat visitors.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Exactly 46 different residents attended every evening.">Exactly 46 different residents attended every evening.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="All 120 registered adults attended every day.">All 120 registered adults attended every day.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The 68 survey respondents chose to participate, so their percentages cannot represent every user or resident." data-hint="Use the voluntary sample to infer a limit, not to erase the responses." data-fix="The voluntary sample cannot represent every user or resident."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which inference from the survey design is defensible?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The 68 survey respondents chose to participate, so their percentages cannot represent every user or resident.">The 68 survey respondents chose to participate, so their percentages cannot represent every user or resident.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The voluntary survey proves every resident had a quieter workspace.">The voluntary survey proves every resident had a quieter workspace.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Because the sample was voluntary, none of the answers existed.">Because the sample was voluntary, none of the answers existed.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The record did not measure employment, income, course completion, or exam results." data-hint="Choose the four explicitly unmeasured outcomes." data-fix="The record did not measure employment, income, course completion, or exam results."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which evidence limit blocks a conclusion about employment or exam outcomes?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The record did not measure employment, income, course completion, or exam results.">The record did not measure employment, income, course completion, or exam results.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The hub proved that every user found employment.">The hub proved that every user found employment.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The survey measured all four outcomes with a control site.">The survey measured all four outcomes with a control site.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="A grant paid $20,000 and the city paid $8,400 of the $28,400 cost; future grant funding is unconfirmed." data-hint="Keep the total, both contributions, and future uncertainty." data-fix="The eight-week trial cost $28,400: $20,000 from a grant and $8,400 from the city, with no confirmed future grant."><p class="quiz-question">6. Which funding summary supports a qualified cost argument?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="A grant paid $20,000 and the city paid $8,400 of the $28,400 cost; future grant funding is unconfirmed.">A grant paid $20,000 and the city paid $8,400 of the $28,400 cost; future grant funding is unconfirmed.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The city permanently guaranteed every future cost.">The city permanently guaranteed every future cost.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The trial cost $8,400 and had no grant support.">The trial cost $8,400 and had no grant support.</button></div></div>
