  <h2>Notice and repair the broken discourse signal</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="despite" data-hint="A finite clause follows the concessive word." data-fix="Although the survey was voluntary, it identified useful questions." data-why="Despite takes a noun phrase or -ing form unless it is followed by the fact that; although directly introduces a finite clause." data-success-message="Correct. The concessive subordinator now matches the full clause."><h3>Repair 1: clause after a preposition</h3><p>Tap the marker whose complement is wrong.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="despite">Despite</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="survey">the survey was voluntary,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="identified">it identified</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="questions">useful questions.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="however" data-hint="A comma alone cannot normally join these two independent clauses with a sentence connector." data-fix="The trial was short. However, it revealed a useful pattern." data-why="Use a period or semicolon before contrastive however and a comma after its opening position." data-success-message="Correct. The sentence connector now has a complete boundary before it and a comma after it."><h3>Repair 2: comma splice</h3><p>Tap the connector that needs a stronger boundary.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="trial">The trial was short,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="however">however</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="revealed">it revealed</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="pattern">a useful pattern.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="contrary" data-hint="The second site has a different advantage; it does not deny that the annex is central." data-fix="The annex is centrally located. By contrast, the north site has more parking." data-why="On the contrary rejects a proposition directly. By contrast compares two distinct cases." data-success-message="Correct. The comparison marker now preserves both site descriptions."><h3>Repair 3: contrast versus direct rejection</h3><p>Tap the marker that falsely denies the first claim.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="annex">The annex is centrally located.</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="contrary">On the contrary,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="north">the north site</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="parking">has more parking.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="therefore" data-hint="The record did not measure employment and had no comparison site." data-fix="Attendance averaged 46 visits per evening. The trial did not measure employment outcomes." data-why="Therefore presents the next proposition as an inference, but attendance alone cannot establish employment impact. Remove the unsupported causal bridge." data-success-message="Correct. The revision reports both facts without manufacturing a causal conclusion."><h3>Repair 4: connector stronger than the evidence</h3><p>Tap the marker that creates an unsupported inference.</p><div class="spot-options"><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="attendance">Attendance averaged 46 visits per evening.</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="therefore">Therefore,</button><button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="employment">the hub improved employment outcomes.</button></div><p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p></div>

  <h2>Say the logical move before you reveal it</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-transform><p class="note-line">Respond aloud first. Name the relation, state the evidence, select a marker, and place the thought-group boundary. Then reveal and compare.</p><div class="transform-list">
    <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>1</b> Grant the voluntary survey limit, then preserve its value as a source of questions.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>Admittedly, the survey was voluntary. Nevertheless, it identified questions worth testing.</strong></p></div>
    <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>2</b> Compare the annex's transit access with the north site's parking.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The annex is near three bus routes, whereas the north site has more parking.</strong></p></div>
    <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>3</b> Reject the claim that the hub was empty.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The hub was not empty. On the contrary, it averaged 46 visits per evening.</strong></p></div>
    <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>4</b> Infer the limit created by the lack of a comparison site.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>The trial had no comparison site. Therefore, it cannot establish that the hub caused later outcomes.</strong></p></div>
    <div class="transform-item" data-transform-item><p class="transform-cue"><b>5</b> Give the weighed conclusion with no claim of permanence.</p><button class="lesson-btn" data-reveal-transform>Reveal after you answer</button><p class="transform-answer" data-transform-answer><strong>On balance, a measured twelve-month extension at the same annex is defensible.</strong></p></div>
  </div></div>

  <h2>Practice argumentation without exposing private positions</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p>You never need to discuss a real political affiliation, employer dispute, medical decision, financial hardship, immigration case, disability, academic record, legal conflict, or family disagreement. Use Westbridge or a tutor-created file. The skill is transparent reasoning, not pressure to defend a personal belief.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Relation map:</b> Write six source propositions. Draw an arrow only when one adds, contrasts, concedes, corrects, supports an inference, or reformulates another. Label the arrow before choosing a marker.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Marker swap:</b> Replace <span class="ex">nevertheless</span> with <span class="ex">therefore</span>, <span class="ex">on the contrary</span>, or no marker. Explain how each change alters or breaks the promised relationship.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Position swap:</b> Move <span class="ex">however</span> from initial to medial position. Then build <span class="ex">however + adjective</span>. Explain the changes in syntax, scope, punctuation, and rhythm.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Register swap:</b> Give a formal report with <span class="ex">admittedly, nevertheless, furthermore</span>, then a natural conversation with <span class="ex">sure, still, also</span>. Preserve the evidence and strength.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Density edit:</b> Draft six marked sentences. Remove at least two markers while keeping the hierarchy clear through order, reference, repetition, and paragraph structure.</div>

  <h2>Final production and check</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card"><h3>Final production: deliver a two-minute evidence map</h3><p>Use Westbridge or a new fictional record with at least six sourced facts. State a position, concede one relevant limitation, preserve a defensible counterclaim, add independent support, compare two options, reject one directly false proposition, draw one warranted inference, give an example, reformulate the scope, and reach a weighed conclusion.</p><p>Use one sentence connector, one semicolon pattern, one medial parenthetical, one subordinator, one prepositional concession, one <span class="ex">however + adjective</span> clause, one <span class="ex">thereby + -ing</span> result, and one parallel pair. Include a formal version and a conversational version. Remove one marker because the relation is already clear. Your listener challenges one arrow or source; qualify or remove the marker immediately.</p><p><b>Listener check:</b> Can the listener identify each promised relation, its two connected propositions, the grammatical scope of the marker, the evidence supporting the bridge, the register, the thought-group boundary, and the final degree of certainty?</p></div>
  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You preserved exact relations, form, punctuation, register, spoken prominence, and evidence strength across the complete argument."><h3>Seven final decisions</h3><div class="quiz-list">
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Admittedly, the evidence is limited. Nevertheless, it justifies a larger trial." data-hint="The B2 assessment grants a limitation, then preserves a proportionate next step." data-fix="Admittedly, the evidence is limited. Nevertheless, it justifies a larger trial."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which pair matches the B2 exit-assessment logic?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Admittedly, the evidence is limited. Nevertheless, it justifies a larger trial.">Admittedly, the evidence is limited. Nevertheless, it justifies a larger trial.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Therefore, the evidence is limited. On the contrary, larger trial.">Therefore, the evidence is limited. On the contrary, larger trial.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Despite the evidence is limited, but it justifies.">Despite the evidence is limited, but it justifies.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The annex is near three bus routes, whereas the north site has more parking." data-hint="Compare different advantages without denying either one." data-fix="The annex is near three bus routes, whereas the north site has more parking."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence makes an accurate comparison?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The annex is near three bus routes, whereas the north site has more parking.">The annex is near three bus routes, whereas the north site has more parking.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The annex is near three bus routes. On the contrary, the north site has parking.">The annex is near three bus routes. On the contrary, the north site has parking.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Whereas the annex near buses, therefore parking.">Whereas the annex near buses, therefore parking.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="However short the trial was, it revealed a useful attendance pattern." data-hint="Use the no-matter-how concessive degree pattern without a comma after however." data-fix="However short the trial was, it revealed a useful attendance pattern."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which sentence uses <span class="ex">however + adjective</span> accurately?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="However short the trial was, it revealed a useful attendance pattern.">However short the trial was, it revealed a useful attendance pattern.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="However, short the trial was, it revealed a pattern.">However, short the trial was, it revealed a pattern.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="However the short trial, but it revealed.">However the short trial, but it revealed.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The city added evening hours, thereby improving access for daytime workers." data-hint="Thereby links the action to its resulting mechanism and takes an -ing form." data-fix="The city added evening hours, thereby improving access for daytime workers."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which sentence uses <span class="ex">thereby</span> accurately?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The city added evening hours, thereby improving access for daytime workers.">The city added evening hours, thereby improving access for daytime workers.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The city added evening hours. Thereby, access improved maybe.">The city added evening hours. Thereby, access improved maybe.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Thereby the city to improve access evening.">Thereby the city to improve access evening.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The hub was not empty. On the contrary, it averaged 46 visits per evening." data-hint="Reject the directly false empty claim with opposing evidence." data-fix="The hub was not empty. On the contrary, it averaged 46 visits per evening."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which context licenses <span class="ex">on the contrary</span>?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The hub was not empty. On the contrary, it averaged 46 visits per evening.">The hub was not empty. On the contrary, it averaged 46 visits per evening.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The annex is central. On the contrary, the other site has more parking.">The annex is central. On the contrary, the other site has more parking.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The cost was recorded. On the contrary, the schedule began at six.">The cost was recorded. On the contrary, the schedule began at six.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The voluntary sample cannot represent every user; therefore, any population percentage must remain qualified." data-hint="The sample design supports a limit on generalization, not a claim that the responses are worthless." data-fix="The voluntary sample cannot represent every user; therefore, any population percentage must remain qualified."><p class="quiz-question">6. Which inference is proportionate to the evidence?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The voluntary sample cannot represent every user; therefore, any population percentage must remain qualified.">The voluntary sample cannot represent every user; therefore, any population percentage must remain qualified.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Attendance rose; therefore, the hub created jobs for every user.">Attendance rose; therefore, the hub created jobs for every user.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The marker therefore proves the next claim even without data.">The marker therefore proves the next claim even without data.</button></div></div>
    <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Use a marker only when it clarifies a relationship the propositions and evidence already support." data-hint="Treat signposting as a map of reasoning, not a substitute for reasoning." data-fix="Use a marker only when it clarifies a supported relationship."><p class="quiz-question">7. Which final principle produces advanced, readable discourse?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Use a marker only when it clarifies a relationship the propositions and evidence already support.">Use a marker only when it clarifies a relationship the propositions and evidence already support.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Place the longest possible marker in every sentence.">Place the longest possible marker in every sentence.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Choose formal markers first and invent the logic later.">Choose formal markers first and invent the logic later.</button></div></div>
  </div><div class="drill-actions"><button class="lesson-btn" data-check-quiz>Check</button><button class="lesson-btn" data-reset-quiz>Reset</button></div><p class="feedback" data-feedback></p></div>

  <h2>Reflect: can every signpost defend its promise?</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card"><h3>Explain the discourse architecture</h3><p>Complete these lines aloud: <span class="ex">The two propositions are...</span> <span class="ex">Their exact relation is...</span> <span class="ex">The source licenses that bridge because...</span> <span class="ex">This marker takes a clause / phrase / sentence...</span> <span class="ex">Its scope is...</span> <span class="ex">Its punctuation is...</span> <span class="ex">Its register is...</span> <span class="ex">The thought-group boundary falls...</span> <span class="ex">A simpler marker or no marker would be better if...</span></p><p>Then remove the source, change the relation, move the marker, or switch from a report to a conversation. Reformulate immediately and explain what must change.</p><p><a href="#next-day-retrieval">Return tomorrow for the five-item retrieval check</a> before rereading the lesson.</p></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Next use:</b> Take one short public-information paragraph or tutor-created file. Underline every signpost, label its two propositions and relation, remove one unnecessary marker, and justify one warranted inference.</div>
  <section id="next-day-retrieval" data-lesson-extension="Next-day concession pair, direct correction, concessive however, thereby form, and evidence-bound inference retrieval"><h2>Next-day retrieval</h2><div class="lead-rule"></div><p>Return without rereading. Reconstruct relation, form, position, register, and evidence strength in five new fictional contexts.</p>
    <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You retained the concession pair, direct correction, however degree pattern, thereby form, and evidence-bound inference."><h3>Five delayed decisions</h3><div class="quiz-list">
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Admittedly, the inspection covered only two rooms. Nevertheless, it identified a pattern worth testing building-wide." data-hint="Grant the narrow scope first, then preserve a proportionate next step despite it." data-fix="Admittedly, the inspection covered only two rooms. Nevertheless, it identified a pattern worth testing building-wide."><p class="quiz-question">1. Which pair concedes the sample limit and supports further testing?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Admittedly, the inspection covered only two rooms. Nevertheless, it identified a pattern worth testing building-wide.">Admittedly, the inspection covered only two rooms. Nevertheless, it identified a pattern worth testing building-wide.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Therefore, two rooms. On the contrary, building-wide proved.">Therefore, two rooms. On the contrary, building-wide proved.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Despite the inspection covered two rooms, but the pattern.">Despite the inspection covered two rooms, but the pattern.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The service was not slower. On the contrary, the median wait fell from nine minutes to six." data-hint="Reject the slower claim directly with the recorded opposite." data-fix="The service was not slower. On the contrary, the median wait fell from nine minutes to six."><p class="quiz-question">2. Which sentence licenses direct correction?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The service was not slower. On the contrary, the median wait fell from nine minutes to six.">The service was not slower. On the contrary, the median wait fell from nine minutes to six.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The service costs less. On the contrary, the office has blue walls.">The service costs less. On the contrary, the office has blue walls.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The service was slower, on the contrary the wait.">The service was slower, on the contrary the wait.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="However narrow the sample was, it revealed a question worth investigating." data-hint="Build no-matter-how plus adjective, subject, and verb, with no comma after however." data-fix="However narrow the sample was, it revealed a question worth investigating."><p class="quiz-question">3. Which concessive degree clause is complete?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="However narrow the sample was, it revealed a question worth investigating.">However narrow the sample was, it revealed a question worth investigating.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="However, narrow the sample was, it revealed a question.">However, narrow the sample was, it revealed a question.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Despite the sample was narrow, but question.">Despite the sample was narrow, but question.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="The clinic added evening appointments, thereby allowing daytime workers to attend." data-hint="Use thereby followed by an -ing form to name the result produced by the added hours." data-fix="The clinic added evening appointments, thereby allowing daytime workers to attend."><p class="quiz-question">4. Which sentence expresses a resulting means accurately?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The clinic added evening appointments, thereby allowing daytime workers to attend.">The clinic added evening appointments, thereby allowing daytime workers to attend.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="The clinic added appointments. Thereby, workers attended maybe.">The clinic added appointments. Thereby, workers attended maybe.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Thereby the clinic to allow daytime attend.">Thereby the clinic to allow daytime attend.</button></div></div>
      <div class="quiz-item" data-quiz-item data-answer="Use therefore only if the documented premise supports the inference, and qualify or remove it when the bridge is uncertain." data-hint="The marker displays an inference but does not supply its missing evidence." data-fix="Use therefore only when the documented premise supports the inference."><p class="quiz-question">5. Which rule keeps a result marker responsible?</p><div class="quiz-options"><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Use therefore only if the documented premise supports the inference, and qualify or remove it when the bridge is uncertain.">Use therefore only if the documented premise supports the inference, and qualify or remove it when the bridge is uncertain.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Therefore turns any later statement into a proven fact.">Therefore turns any later statement into a proven fact.</button><button class="quiz-option" data-quiz-option="Formal punctuation replaces the need for a documented premise.">Formal punctuation replaces the need for a documented premise.</button></div></div>
